ModelReturned: f{"ResponseMetadata": {"RequestId": "ed78910c-69d5-411f-a6a4-e3929496a4e5", "HTTPStatusCode": 200, "HTTPHeaders": {"date": "Wed, 10 Sep 2025 18:23:47 GMT", "content-type": "application/json", "content-length": "1547", "connection": "keep-alive", "x-amzn-requestid": "ed78910c-69d5-411f-a6a4-e3929496a4e5"}, "RetryAttempts": 0}, "output": {"message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "<thinking>\nThe Jira ticket TRC-28931 reports an application stuck in the provisioning stage with phone number 7329414634. To resolve this:\n\n1. Need to identify the application ID associated with this phone number\n2. Verify the application's current status and provisioning stage details\n3. Check for technical errors in the provisioning stage\n\nFirst step: Find the application ID using the provided phone number from the contactDetails section. The schema shows contactDetails.details contains \"phoneNumber\" which matches the ticket's description. The database relationship requires joining application_section to application to get the main application record.\n\nKey considerations:\n- Must use database_id=7 as per schema\n- Apply LIMIT 9 to comply with query guidelines\n- Need to handle phone number formatting (ticket shows 10 digits, schema example uses +91 prefix)\n\nNext step: Execute SQL query to find application ID by phone number while respecting data privacy requirements.\n</thinking>\n\n"}, {"toolUse": {"toolUseId": "tooluse_LkW9sfITTGSrDSJ3gWBVMQ", "name": "execute_query", "input": {"database_id": 7, "query": "SELECT a.id AS application_id, a.status, a.spool_id, s.details \nFROM application a\nJOIN application_section s ON a.id = s.application_id\nWHERE s.name = 'contactDetails'\nAND s.details->>'phoneNumber' = '7329414634'\nLIMIT 9;"}}}]}}, "stopReason": "tool_use", "usage": {"inputTokens": 5505, "outputTokens": 330, "totalTokens": 5835}, "metrics": {"latencyMs": 12193}}


